  "summary": "Adds 0-of-0 OP_CHECKMULTISIG and OP_CHECKMULTISIGVERIFY test cases for tapscript in feature_taproot.py to verify that failure is triggered specifically by the opcode ban rather than DER signature validation errors. Also dumps the expected error string for failure cases into the test assets and verifies in script_assets_tests that evaluation fails with the exact expected script error code under the declared flags.",
  "problem": "Existing tapscript test cases for disabled CHECKMULTISIG opcodes supplied Schnorr signatures, which fail DER signature validation when the opcode is executed. As a result, an implementation that incorrectly executes CHECKMULTISIG in tapscript still passed all tests. Additionally, the script asset test runner only verified that a test failed, without ensuring it failed for the correct reason.",
